  "comments": [
    {
      "position": 0,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "V-dic + 〜\n食べるにつれて　 along with eating\n\nNoun + 〜\n増加につれて along with the increase",
      "html": "V-dic + 〜<br/>食べるにつれて　 along with eating<br/><br/>Noun + 〜<br/>増加につれて along with the increase",
      "credits_raw": "dc",
      "content_sha256": "00a932deadebfbf80a566466bcfd18786c6b4947ea50927b0134026c08e94042",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 1,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "連れて行く means to take someone with (you)\n\n私は友達を連れて行きました\nI took my friend along\n\nWill you take us for a drive next Sunday?\n今度の日曜日にドライブにつれていってくれませんか。",
      "html": "連れて行く means to take someone with (you)<br/><br/>私は友達を連れて行きました<br/>I took my friend along<br/><br/>Will you take us for a drive next Sunday?<br/>今度の日曜日にドライブにつれていってくれませんか。",
      "credits_raw": "dc",
      "content_sha256": "f81c789f968827909121e12a5e1dde1cb5e8cab117f76b8abe691d8a00fd8cf2",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "＊につれ(て) is a phrase used to indicate that a change occurs in accordance with another simultaneous change. Because of this, the verbs in the につれ(て) clause and the main clause have to be verbs of change or of a process, such as 'become proficient' and 'increase.'\n\n＊When と共に(とともに) means 'as,' it can be rephrased as につれて, に伴って(にともなって), or に従って(にしたがって).\nEXAMPLE: 景気の回復[と共に/につれて/に伴って/に従って]失業率が下がってきた。(As business recovers, the unemployment rate is coming down.)\n\n＊The difference between Ｖ(inf・nonpast)にしたがって and Ｖ(inf・nonpast)につれて is that the former is more of a written style and the latter is more of a spoken style.\n\nFORMATION:\nＶ(inf・nonpast) + につれて\nＮ + につれて",
      "html": "＊につれ(て) is a phrase used to indicate that a change occurs in accordance with another simultaneous change. Because of this, the verbs in the につれ(て) clause and the main clause have to be verbs of change or of a process, such as 'become proficient' and 'increase.'<br/><br/>＊When と共に(とともに) means 'as,' it can be rephrased as につれて, に伴って(にともなって), or に従って(にしたがって).<br/>EXAMPLE: 景気の回復[と共に/につれて/に伴って/に従って]失業率が下がってきた。(As business recovers, the unemployment rate is coming down.)<br/><br/>＊The difference between Ｖ(inf・nonpast)にしたがって and Ｖ(inf・nonpast)につれて is that the former is more of a written style and the latter is more of a spoken style.<br/><br/>FORMATION:<br/>Ｖ(inf・nonpast) + につれて<br/>Ｎ + につれて",
      "credits_raw": "rubyhatchet",
      "content_sha256": "8b6cee9cf46b0483e103dc369e2b643651ff765c1bc774b1a541d02f00a271c7",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "It seems like Nitsurete is often accompanied by -kita at the end of the sentence.",
      "html": "It seems like Nitsurete is often accompanied by -kita at the end of the sentence.",
      "credits_raw": "nhk9",
      "content_sha256": "0b20d39273d41671901ee3bc069d46765f4f9d4bcff18bd72541b5e3afeb02fa",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "nitsurete can be replaced by nitomonatte.\nnitusrete has a nuance of degree.\n As I ate (more and more), ...\n As one reads something (more), ...",
      "html": "nitsurete can be replaced by nitomonatte.<br/>nitusrete has a nuance of degree.<br/> As I ate (more and more), ...<br/> As one reads something (more), ...",
      "credits_raw": "Miki",
      "content_sha256": "5f7aa7364e6b166d663ff98c19ddbae872a99db6ad28389cf874dc9b8b994fdf",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "But -kita at the end suggests you eye-witness the changes?",
      "html": "But -kita at the end suggests you eye-witness the changes?",
      "credits_raw": "author",
      "content_sha256": "663a2fa8bf343e46131232e59ff7d6db12d6798fb8f3f8bec60a2e3a34079c6b",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "are niturete, nitomatte, totomoni and nishitagatte fundamentally the same in usage?",
      "html": "are niturete, nitomatte, totomoni and nishitagatte fundamentally the same in usage?",
      "credits_raw": "sagittarius",
      "content_sha256": "ad1567827be2524f72d9f5d2abbd2a0ae3168ce944d675696039ad3a093a3886",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "No kita doesnt suggest that you have eye witnessed it but just suggests that something has come to be.\neg. 寒くなって来た。 It has gotten colder.",
      "html": "No kita doesnt suggest that you have eye witnessed it but just suggests that something has come to be.<br/>eg. 寒くなって来た。 It has gotten colder.",
      "credits_raw": "cbee",
      "content_sha256": "f94a8d2931967ae31f99fb10e264a4ebc4177fd31cbf489dff517af4adedcf6d",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "so totomoni and nitsurete are interchangable?",
      "html": "so totomoni and nitsurete are interchangable?",
      "credits_raw": "karekora",
      "content_sha256": "7248fe4723c1be601a02160a36e9f71812372b87d3f5f6081949ca796e323e2a",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
